// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/stacked_method.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The frozen first model supplies targets for stage two. Only after exact transfer are all four layers optimized together. Scratch uses a separate full stack and fewer total data passes.)
\alttext(Ordered training stages show a shallow pixel model, frozen representation cache, shallow latent model, transfer of eight arrays, and joint reconstruction of original pixels.)

`models::SigmoidAutoencoder` supplies the reusable forward computation for every geometry.
Its integer widths are positive, mirrored and strictly decreasing into the central code. Every
layer is sigmoid with independent Glorot weights and zero biases, named `layer<i>/W,b`.
`SigmoidAutoencoderDecode` takes only explicit codes and the complete geometry, retaining
original decoder layer indices. Both functions keep gradients and owning tensor handles;
they contain no optimizer, transfer or stage-selection policy.

> A hand-checkable four-layer stack

Take widths [4,3,2,3,4], input [0.2,0.4,0.6,0.8], every weight 0.1 and every bias 0. Because
all units in a layer have equal weights, its repeated activities satisfy
\(a_1=\sigma(0.2)\), \(a_2=\sigma(0.3a_1)\), \(a_3=\sigma(0.2a_2)\) and
\(a_4=\sigma(0.3a_3)\). This deliberately degenerate example teaches composition, not useful
feature learning. It has eight learned leaves and 48 scalars. The program checks every activity
against the scalar formulas and exact standalone two-layer decoding.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/stacked_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n            = dm::nn;
  const auto        type = n::DType::Float64;
  const n::Shape    widths{4, 3, 2, 3, 4};
  n::ParameterStore p(1543, type);
  const auto        x = n::tensor({.2, .4, .6, .8}, {1, 4}, type);
  {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    n::models::SigmoidAutoencoder(p, x, widths);
  }
  for (const auto& name : p.names())
    p.set(name, n::full(p.at(name).shape(), name.ends_with("/W") ? .1 : 0., type));
  const auto   layers  = n::models::SigmoidAutoencoder(p, x, widths);
  auto         sigmoid = [](double z) { return 1 / (1 + std::exp(-z)); };
  const double a1 = sigmoid(.2), a2 = sigmoid(.3 * a1), a3 = sigmoid(.2 * a2),
               a4 = sigmoid(.3 * a3);
  const std::vector<double> expected{a1, a2, a3, a4};
  std::print("| layer | width | repeated activity |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(58, 1100);
  d.node("x", {0, 0}, "Input: 4 values\nSum = 2")
      .node("h", {5, 0}, std::format("3 sigmoid units\na1 = {:.6f}", a1))
      .node("z", {10, 0}, std::format("2 code units\na2 = {:.6f}", a2))
      .node("r", {10, -3}, std::format("3 decoder units\na3 = {:.6f}", a3))
      .node("o", {5, -3}, std::format("4 output units\na4 = {:.6f}", a4))
      .edge("x", "h")
      .edge("h", "z")
      .edge("z", "r")
      .edge("r", "o");
  for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
    if (n::max(n::abs(layers[i] - expected[i])).item() > 1e-14)
      return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.9f} |\n", i, widths[i + 1], expected[i]);
  }
  if (p.count() != 48 ||
      n::max(n::abs(n::models::SigmoidAutoencoderDecode(p, layers[1], widths) - layers.back()))
              .item() != 0)
    return 1;
  const auto loss      = n::mean(n::square(layers.back() - x));
  const auto gradients = n::grad(loss, p.parameters());
  for (const auto& g : gradients)
    if (!std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(g)).item()) || n::sum(n::square(g)).item() <= 0)
      return 1;
  d.save_svg("build/stacked_toy.svg");
  std::print("Pixel MSE {:.9f}; all eight gradient tensors finite and nonzero.\n", loss.item());
}
```
