Pixel MSE 0.051555922; all eight gradient tensors finite and nonzero.
\image(figures/stacked_toy.svg)
// result_end

\caption(Repeated activities arise from equal toy weights, not from a gate or parameter sharing. The full model keeps independent weight matrices at every layer.)
\alttext(Four sigmoid layers of widths three, two, three and four show scalar activities computed from a four-coordinate input and constant 0.1 weights.)

For any layer \(H_{l+1}=\sigma(H_lW_l+b_l)\), the output preactivation derivative for
\(L=\operatorname{MSE}(H_L,X)\) is
\(\Delta_L=2(H_L-X)\odot H_L\odot(1-H_L)/(Bd)\). Earlier deltas are
\(\Delta_l=(\Delta_{l+1}W_l^\top)\odot H_l\odot(1-H_l)\), with weight derivatives
\(\partial L/\partial W_l=H_l^\top\Delta_{l+1}\) and matching bias row sums. Greedy stage two uses Y as its target and
normalizes by B×64, while full reconstruction normalizes by B×784. In joint fitting gradients
traverse all four layers; during greedy stage two the cached Y has no gradient path to stage one.

The source's separate 4–3–2–3–4 sinusoidal-weight fixture is retained in native tests: all 24
activities and all 48 weight/bias derivatives are compared with independent scalar chain rules.
Additional Float64 finite differences test every parameter, input and second derivative.

> The executed full graph and exact transfer map

Stage one has 101, 200 scalars, stage two 2,128, and the full stack 103,328 in eight leaves.
The full layer counts are 50,240, 1,040, 1,088 and 50,960. Geometry is symmetric; decoder matrices
are independent, not tied transposes. A one-image shape probe executes the full graph with named
layer boundaries. Graph style, Blocks detail, linear scales, a two-pixel visibility floor,
six sampled planes and eight sampled neurons preserve the 784–64–16–64–784 shapes in labels.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/stacked_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore p(1553);
  const n::Shape    widths{784, 64, 16, 64, 784};
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& x) {
        const auto                     layers = n::models::SigmoidAutoencoder(p, x, widths);
        auto                           previous = x;
        const std::vector<std::string> labels{
            "Encoder 1: 784 → 64",
            "Encoder 2: code 16",
            "Decoder 2: 16 → 64",
            "Decoder 1: raw pixels"};
        for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
          n::model_stage(labels[i], previous, layers[i]);
          previous = layers[i];
        }
        return layers.back();
      },
      "All-sigmoid stacked autoencoder: untied 784–64–16–64–784");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Graph;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.max_neurons           = 8;
  options.sizing.spatial_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.channel_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 6;
  const auto figure             = model.plot(n::zeros({1, 784}), options);
  if (p.count() != 103328 || p.size() != 8 || figure.parameter_count() != 103328)
    return 1;
  figure.save_svg("build/stacked_architecture.svg");
  std::print("| full-stack parameter | scalars |\n|---|---:|\n");
  for (const auto& name : p.names())
    std::print("| {} | {} |\n", name, p.at(name).numel());
}
```
