\caption(The sixteen-value code is the sole bridge to the two learned decoder layers. Shared drawing scales show geometry; every matrix remains independently trainable during joint fitting.)
\alttext(A traced tensor graph shows four sigmoid blocks, narrowing from 784 to 64 to 16 and expanding through 64 back to784, with 103328 learned scalars.)

| full-stack layer | selected source layer | role |
|---|---|---|
| layer0 | stage1/layer0 | first encoder |
| layer1 | stage2/layer0 | second encoder |
| layer2 | stage2/layer1 | second decoder |
| layer3 | stage1/layer1 | first decoder |

Both W and b transfer for each row. Existing full-stack leaves are overwritten in place with
`ParameterStore::set`, preserving the already-created optimizer's references. Values copy into
independent initialized storage, so later joint updates cannot mutate frozen stages. Transfer
checks cover all names, shapes, dtypes and value bytes. The optimizer's fresh zero moments are
not copied from either shallow model.

> Genuine MNIST and frozen data partitions

Native preparation loads the original balanced 1,000 fitting, 200 validation and200 test images.
Fit and validation use disjoint official training IDs; test IDs are from the official test split.
Float32 [0,1] pixels flatten without resizing. All phases use the same original source IDs and
record order, even when their target coordinates change. Labels only choose gallery columns.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", cache.string());
  const auto      pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(cache / "saliency");
  n::NamedTensors data;
  std::print("| pool | images | features |\n|---|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
    const std::string name = i == 0 ? "fit" : i == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    data.emplace_back(name + "_images", pools[i].images.reshape({pools[i].images.size(0), 784}));
    data.emplace_back(name + "_source_ids", pools[i].source);
    if (i == 2)
      data.emplace_back("test_labels", pools[i].labels);
    std::print("| {} | {} | 784 |\n", name, pools[i].images.size(0));
  }
  n::save_npz("build/stacked_data.npz", data);
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "saliency" / "manifest.json",
      "build/stacked_data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}
