\caption(Each curve has its own starting weights. Stage-two validation MSE is in 64-dimensional frozen representation space and is deliberately absent from this pixel-MSE plot.)
\alttext(Validation pixel losses show the first shallow model, joint fine-tuning from transferred weights and the scratch stack. Scratch reaches its minimum at epoch two.)

The source selections are stage1/stage2/fine-tune/scratch = 3/3/3/2. Joint phases each receive 96
updates, but the staged route additionally trains two shallow models: 288 updates and nine data
passes in total versus 96 updates and three passes for scratch. Model sizes differ across those
passes, so step counts are not measured floating-point work or wall-clock speed ratios. This
comparison holds the joint phase fixed; it cannot attribute all differences to pretraining alone.

> Decoder composition and an error bound

After transfer the full reconstruction is exactly \(g_1(g_2(f_2(f_1(X))))\), including both
learned decoders. With Y=f1(X), R1=X−g1(Y) and R2=Y−g2(f2(Y)), the triangle inequality gives

$$
\|X-g_1(g_2(f_2(Y)))\|_F\le\|R_1\|_F+L_{g_1}\|R_2\|_F,\qquad
L_{g_1}\le\tfrac14\|W_{g_1}\|_2\le\tfrac14\|W_{g_1}\|_F.
$$
\alttext(Composed pixel error is bounded by first-stage pixel error plus first-decoder sensitivity times second-stage representation error. A sigmoid's maximum slope gives the decoder Lipschitz bound.)

Dividing by \(\sqrt{Bd}\) yields
\(\operatorname{RMSE}_{pre}\le\operatorname{RMSE}_1+
\tfrac14\|W_{g_1}\|_F\sqrt{64/784}\operatorname{RMSE}_{stage2}\).
This loose but checkable bound explains why a small latent MSE does not guarantee a better
pixel reconstruction: the losses have different coordinates, scales and decoder sensitivity.
It is a bound for the frozen transferred model, not a convergence or fine-tuning guarantee.

The next program restores a fresh fine-tuned stack, checks exact code/reconstruction and
standalone decoding, single-versus-batch agreement within 1e-6, and immutable weights. It then
scores the frozen pretrained model, fine-tuning, scratch, fitting mean, shifted codes and zero
codes against the same original held-out pixels. No control is refitted.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> data, cache, pre;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz("build/stacked_data.npz"))
    data.emplace(key, value);
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz("build/stacked_cache.npz"))
    cache.emplace(key, value);
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz("build/stacked_pretrained.npz"))
    pre.emplace(key, value);
  const n::Shape    shallow{784, 64, 784}, deep{784, 64, 16, 64, 784};
  n::ParameterStore first(1549), fine(1553), scratch(1553), deployed(1553);
  first.load("build/stacked_stage1_best.npz", false);
  fine.load("build/stacked_finetune_best.npz", false);
  scratch.load("build/stacked_scratch_best.npz", false);
  deployed.load("build/stacked_finetune_best.npz", false);
  const auto     before = deployed.flatten();
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  const auto     test         = data.at("test_images");
  const auto     first_result = n::models::SigmoidAutoencoder(first, test, shallow),
             a                = n::models::SigmoidAutoencoder(fine, test, deep),
             b                = n::models::SigmoidAutoencoder(scratch, test, deep),
             restored         = n::models::SigmoidAutoencoder(deployed, test, deep);
  if (!n::equal_bits(restored[1], a[1]) || !n::equal_bits(restored[3], a[3]) ||
      !n::equal_bits(n::models::SigmoidAutoencoderDecode(deployed, restored[1], deep), restored[3]))
    return 1;
  const auto single = n::models::SigmoidAutoencoder(deployed, n::take_rows(test, {0}), deep);
  if (n::max(n::abs(single.back() - n::take_rows(restored.back(), {0}))).item() > 1e-6)
    return 1;
  const auto shuffled = n::models::SigmoidAutoencoderDecode(
      deployed,
      n::concat({n::slice_axis(restored[1], 0, 1, 200), n::slice_axis(restored[1], 0, 0, 1)}, 0),
      deep);
  const auto zero = n::models::SigmoidAutoencoderDecode(deployed, n::zeros({200, 16}), deep);
  const auto mean = n::broadcast_to(
      n::cast(
          n::mean(n::cast(data.at("fit_images"), n::DType::Float64), {0}, true), n::DType::Float32),
      test.shape());
  auto score = [](const n::Tensor& x, const n::Tensor& target) {
    return n::mean(n::square(n::cast(x, n::DType::Float64) - n::cast(target, n::DType::Float64)))
        .item();
  };
  std::print("| reconstruction | held-out pixel MSE |\n|---|---:|\n");
  for (const auto& [name, value] : n::NamedTensors{
           {"first shallow model", first_result.back()},
           {"transferred pretrained stack", pre.at("reconstruction")},
           {"joint fine-tuning", a.back()},
           {"scratch", b.back()},
           {"fitting mean", mean},
           {"shifted fine-tuned codes", shuffled},
           {"zero fine-tuned codes", zero}})
    std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n", name, score(value, test));
  const double rmse1 = std::sqrt(score(first_result.back(), test)),
               rmse2 =
                   std::sqrt(score(pre.at("stage2_test_reconstruction"), cache.at("test_code"))),
               decoder_norm =
                   n::sqrt(n::sum(n::square(n::cast(first.at("layer1/W"), n::DType::Float64))))
                       .item();
  const double bound  = rmse1 + decoder_norm * .25 * std::sqrt(64. / 784) * rmse2,
               actual = std::sqrt(score(pre.at("reconstruction"), test));
  if (actual > bound + 1e-6 || before != deployed.flatten())
    return 1;
  std::print(
      "Pretrained RMSE {:.9f} <= bound {:.9f}; stage1 RMSE {:.9f}, latent stage2 RMSE {:.9f}, "
      "decoder Frobenius norm {:.9f}.\nFresh restore/decode/batch and immutable checks pass.\n",
      actual,
      bound,
      rmse1,
      rmse2,
      decoder_norm);
  n::NamedTensors packed;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : data)
    packed.emplace_back(key, value);
  packed.insert(
      packed.end(),
      {{"stage1_fit_code", cache.at("fit_code")},
       {"stage1_validation_code", cache.at("validation_code")},
       {"stage1_test_code", cache.at("test_code")},
       {"stage1_test_reconstruction", first_result.back()},
       {"pretrained_test_code", pre.at("code")},
       {"pretrained_test_reconstruction", pre.at("reconstruction")},
       {"finetuned_test_code", a[1]},
       {"finetuned_test_reconstruction", a.back()},
       {"scratch_test_code", b[1]},
       {"scratch_test_reconstruction", b.back()},
       {"mean_reconstruction", mean},
       {"shuffled_reconstruction", shuffled},
       {"zero_reconstruction", zero}});
  n::save_npz("build/stacked_outputs.npz", packed);
  n::save_npz(
      "build/stacked_bound.npz",
      {{"stage2_test_reconstruction", pre.at("stage2_test_reconstruction")},
       {"actual_rmse", n::full({}, actual, n::DType::Float64)},
       {"bound_rmse", n::full({}, bound, n::DType::Float64)},
       {"decoder_frobenius", n::full({}, decoder_norm, n::DType::Float64)}});
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| reconstruction | held-out pixel MSE |
|---|---:|
| first shallow model | 0.067960857 |
| transferred pretrained stack | 0.068480899 |
| joint fine-tuning | 0.066063591 |
| scratch | 0.068178502 |
| fitting mean | 0.067798074 |
| shifted fine-tuned codes | 0.067734778 |
| zero fine-tuned codes | 0.069448788 |
Pretrained RMSE 0.261688554 <= bound 0.356667868; stage1 RMSE 0.260693033, latent stage2 RMSE 0.085672124, decoder Frobenius norm 15.683604290.
Fresh restore/decode/batch and immutable checks pass.
// result_end

The transferred stack's MSE 0.06848 exceeds the first shallow model's 0.06796, despite the
small representation loss. The checked RMSE bound is deliberately loose: 0.35667 against
actual 0.26169. It describes a worst-case allowance, not an expected reconstruction score.

Fine-tuned test MSE 0.06606 is lower than scratch 0.06818 and the fitting mean 0.06780 in this
run. The transferred model alone gives 0.06848. Shifting fine-tuned codes raises error to 0.06773,
close to the constant mean; zero codes give 0.06945. The code carries some useful alignment, but
reconstructions and controls remain close to broad digit averages. The sixteen Float32 values
are continuous coordinates, not a specified compressed bitstream, generative prior or proof of
classification quality. There is no classification confusion matrix for this reconstruction task.

> Reconstructions without quality filtering

Columns select the first held-out occurrence of each digit 0–9. Rows are original, first shallow
model, transferred pretrained stack, fine-tuned stack, scratch stack, fitting mean, shifted-code
decoder and zero-code decoder. Every panel uses fixed [0,1] grayscale, nearest-neighbour
enlargement and no error amplification. These are raw predictions with no copied pixels.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/stacked_reconstructions.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> saved;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz("build/stacked_outputs.npz"))
    saved.emplace(key, value);
  const auto labels = saved.at("test_labels").to_vector<int>(),
             ids    = saved.at("test_source_ids").to_vector<int>();
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  std::print("| digit | original MNIST source ID |\n|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; ++digit) {
    const auto found = std::find(labels.begin(), labels.end(), digit);
    if (found == labels.end())
      return 1;
    rows.push_back(found - labels.begin());
    std::print("| {} | {} |\n", digit, ids[rows.back()]);
  }
  std::vector<n::Tensor> panels;
  for (const auto& key :
       {"test_images",
        "stage1_test_reconstruction",
        "pretrained_test_reconstruction",
        "finetuned_test_reconstruction",
        "scratch_test_reconstruction",
        "mean_reconstruction",
        "shuffled_reconstruction",
        "zero_reconstruction"})
    panels.push_back(n::take_rows(saved.at(key), rows));
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::concat(panels, 0).reshape({80, 28, 28, 1}),
      "build/stacked_reconstructions.png",
      10,
      0,
      1,
      2,
      .8,
      3);
}
```
