> Verification and limits

The core owns configurable forward layers and standalone decoding; complete stage orchestration
remains in editable C++ and native Python/R loops. Native tests preserve all 24 original toy
activities and 48 analytic derivatives, check every small-model first/second finite difference,
validate geometry before creation and verify decoder-only names/counts. Frozen-cache and transfer
tests confirm that both decoders copy independently and that an optimizer created before
transfer still updates the existing joint leaves. Language tests verify owning list elements,
code gradients, strict integer geometry and standalone decoder handles. All source arrays in
42 report archives agree with the original by dtype, shape and every value byte; the same
42 source archives agree across normal C++, Python and R workflows. The optional independent
NumPy oracle (`scripts/check_stacked_autoencoder.py`) verifies all 309,984 first parameter
derivatives (maximum difference 7.6e-10), four bit-exact first Adam updates and 2,873,600
validation/held-out/control prediction pixels (maximum difference 1.5e-7). It also checks all
sixteen validation histories/checkpoints, the epoch-zero policy, eight transfer arrays, cached
representations (maximum activation difference 2.3e-7) and the RMSE bound. Source and report
scalar histories agree within 1e-12 from differing Float64 reduction order. The check neither
prepares data nor replaces the demonstrated optimizer loops.

This experiment demonstrates actual greedy pretraining and exact composition, not merely a
deep architecture called stacked. Its separate objectives, extra data passes and epoch-zero
selection rule are essential to interpreting the measured result. More training, matched total
computation, multiple seeds and downstream tasks would be additional experiments.

> References

- Y. Bengio, P. Lamblin, D. Popovici and H. Larochelle (NIPS2006),
  [Greedy Layer-Wise Training of Deep Networks](https://papers.nips.cc/paper_files/paper/2006/hash/5da713a690c067105aeb2fae32403405-Abstract.html).
  The staged strategy motivates this smaller all-sigmoid MSE adaptation.
- Y. LeCun, C. Cortes and C. J. C. Burges, [MNIST handwritten digit database](https://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/).
  The native manifest records original files and selected official record IDs.
